1
00:00:00,210 --> 00:00:01,040
I'm coming!

2
00:00:03,250 --> 00:00:04,170
Impossible!

3
00:00:04,250 --> 00:00:05,550
Who is this kid!?

4
00:00:16,310 --> 00:00:18,020
He's the coach of the Japan team!

5
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:25,650
Great. He anticipated Tsubasa's move.

6
00:00:26,020 --> 00:00:29,650
Guys, I'm sorry for barging onto the field without permission!

7
00:00:30,110 --> 00:00:31,360
Forgive me.

8
00:00:32,950 --> 00:00:36,990
You can play for the Japan National Team.

9
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:40,660
Your dribbling was breathtaking, Ozora Tsubasa-kun.

10
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:42,370
Coach.

11
00:00:54,340 --> 00:00:59,270
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

12
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:17,910
EPISODE 39
TSUBASA TAKES OFF

13
00:02:22,170 --> 00:02:24,250
Fire Shot!

14
00:02:31,090 --> 00:02:32,430
Goal!

15
00:02:32,510 --> 00:02:36,430
That was Karl Heinz Schneider's Fire Shot!

16
00:02:38,430 --> 00:02:41,190
Hamburg and Munich were tied in the league.

17
00:02:41,310 --> 00:02:42,730
In this crucial match,

18
00:02:42,810 --> 00:02:46,190
Munich, after going 2 goals down, brought on Schneider in the second half.

19
00:02:46,570 --> 00:02:48,030
That was definitely a great choice.

20
00:02:48,110 --> 00:02:50,700
And they made up one goal, now only one left.

21
00:02:51,360 --> 00:02:52,990
Impressive, Schneider.

22
00:02:53,280 --> 00:02:57,000
Japan's A team was selected, I heard Tsubasa got into the team.

23
00:02:57,500 --> 00:03:01,870
And here I signed a professional contract and sat on the bench.

24
00:03:02,460 --> 00:03:06,500
Damn it. I have to improve, I don't want to fall behind.

25
00:03:08,090 --> 00:03:10,170
That was a dangerous play.

26
00:03:10,260 --> 00:03:14,720
Hamburg goalkeeper Budenski's shoulder is dislocated.

27
00:03:15,220 --> 00:03:16,720
Wakabayashi, you're up.

28
00:03:16,970 --> 00:03:17,890
Yes, coach.

29
00:03:21,390 --> 00:03:24,020
Now, replacing Budenski,

30
00:03:24,110 --> 00:03:28,990
15-year-old Japanese goalkeeper Genzo Wakabayashi enters.

31
00:03:31,110 --> 00:03:32,360
Who could have known?

32
00:03:32,530 --> 00:03:36,080
According to our promise, now our battle begins, Wakabayashi.

33
00:03:36,330 --> 00:03:38,870
Alright, bring it on, Schneider.

34
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:40,750
We're protecting our goal advantage.

35
00:03:42,330 --> 00:03:44,250
This is the final match.

36
00:03:47,130 --> 00:03:49,760
Hamburg is still 1 goal ahead.

37
00:03:50,090 --> 00:03:51,760
Wakabayashi, get ready.

38
00:03:54,180 --> 00:03:56,010
Final Fire!

39
00:04:00,890 --> 00:04:02,230
He caught it!

40
00:04:02,310 --> 00:04:04,690
Munich's equalizing effort came to nothing!

41
00:04:07,820 --> 00:04:09,150
The match is over!

42
00:04:09,530 --> 00:04:13,200
Hamburg's Japanese goalkeeper Genzo Wakabayashi

43
00:04:13,570 --> 00:04:16,660
protected the goal and the winning goal!

44
00:04:16,950 --> 00:04:20,330
And still, Hamburg is ahead.

45
00:04:20,410 --> 00:04:25,000
This is S.G.G., Super Goalkeeper Genzo Wakabayashi.

46
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:27,170
With his first brilliant appearance.

47
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:31,460
I won this time, Schneider.

48
00:04:31,840 --> 00:04:35,010
Next time it won't be like this, Wakabayashi!

49
00:04:35,930 --> 00:04:39,680
Japan, Japan!

50
00:04:40,430 --> 00:04:46,100
Japan's first international match against Paraguay.

51
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:51,360
The stadium is full of fans cheering for Japan.

52
00:04:54,320 --> 00:04:56,200
I wonder where Tsubasa is?

53
00:04:57,160 --> 00:04:59,700
Yes, where did he go?

54
00:05:02,790 --> 00:05:04,910
There they are!

55
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:11,170
When it comes to the Japan team, all attention is on the recent champion.

56
00:05:11,250 --> 00:05:14,470
The most famous player of the National Youth Tournament in France,

57
00:05:14,590 --> 00:05:18,970
and the tournament everyone knows, 15-year-old Ozora Tsubasa.

58
00:05:19,300 --> 00:05:22,220
Why is he talking with the opponents?

59
00:05:22,350 --> 00:05:23,930
Probably testing his language skills.

60
00:05:24,020 --> 00:05:26,730
He's learned a lot of South American language.

61
00:05:26,890 --> 00:05:30,110
So, you want to go to São Paulo, Brazil?

62
00:05:30,190 --> 00:05:32,570
I also play in Brazil.

63
00:05:32,650 --> 00:05:34,990
Maybe one day we'll play together, kid.

64
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:37,740
Definitely, and I look forward to that day.

65
00:05:38,070 --> 00:05:40,490
Alright, let's have a good game today.

66
00:05:40,580 --> 00:05:42,740
Yes, but be gentle with me.

67
00:05:47,250 --> 00:05:52,250
Friendly National Match

68
00:05:47,580 --> 00:05:52,250
Ozora Tsubasa's name is not in the starting 11.

69
00:05:52,340 --> 00:05:55,420
When will Tsubasa enter the game?

70
00:05:55,510 --> 00:05:58,380
I know we are all excited for this match today.

71
00:05:59,010 --> 00:06:02,510
God, Tsubasa isn't in the starting lineup.

72
00:06:03,100 --> 00:06:08,690
But even sitting on the bench is a good experience for Tsubasa.

73
00:06:08,940 --> 00:06:09,770
Right.

74
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:14,780
Now the match is starting! Japan - Paraguay.

75
00:06:15,530 --> 00:06:17,490
And the match has begun.

76
00:06:18,860 --> 00:06:22,160
But Paraguay pressured from the start.

77
00:06:22,870 --> 00:06:24,580
They scored 2 goals in the first half.

78
00:06:24,660 --> 00:06:28,670
And they didn't allow Japan to score against them.

79
00:06:29,620 --> 00:06:33,170
Extraordinary. That's how professionals move.

80
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:37,630
Now I have to face this style of football.

81
00:06:46,140 --> 00:06:52,360
And then, in the 5th minute of the second half, Paraguay scored again.

82
00:06:54,610 --> 00:06:58,360
Hey, you have to put Tsubasa in now.

83
00:06:58,650 --> 00:07:01,740
Tsu-ba-sa! Tsu-ba-sa!

84
00:07:01,820 --> 00:07:04,780
Tsu-ba-sa! Tsu-ba-sa!

85
00:07:04,870 --> 00:07:07,790
Tsu-ba-sa! Tsu-ba-sa!

86
00:07:07,870 --> 00:07:10,830
Tsu-ba-sa! Tsu-ba-sa!

87
00:07:10,920 --> 00:07:13,790
Tsu-ba-sa! Tsu-ba-sa!

88
00:07:13,880 --> 00:07:16,750
Tsu-ba-sa! Tsu-ba-sa!

89
00:07:17,210 --> 00:07:22,840
Wow! Listen, the whole stadium is calling for Tsubasa.

90
00:07:22,930 --> 00:07:26,010
The crowd was waiting for Ozora Tsubasa!

91
00:07:26,100 --> 00:07:30,140
The fans are looking for a new power for Japanese football!

92
00:07:30,940 --> 00:07:34,190
Tsubasa, do you hear? The fans' cheers...

93
00:07:35,150 --> 00:07:38,360
You are the one who will change football in Japan!

94
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:40,280
Only you exist!

95
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:42,780
Go, Tsubasa!

96
00:07:43,910 --> 00:07:44,780
Yes, coach.

97
00:07:52,500 --> 00:07:57,300
Japan wins a throw-in and they announce a substitution.

98
00:07:57,420 --> 00:08:00,050
Ozora Tsubasa enters the field!

99
00:08:00,170 --> 00:08:01,550
Tsubasa has arrived!

100
00:08:01,630 --> 00:08:02,720
Tsubasa!

101
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:04,800
We trust you, Tsubasa!

102
00:08:11,230 --> 00:08:14,810
It seems Tsubasa wants to take the throw-in himself.

103
00:08:15,980 --> 00:08:16,810
Alright!

104
00:08:24,110 --> 00:08:26,910
The ball goes in front of the Paraguay goal.

105
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:28,080
What!?

106
00:08:28,370 --> 00:08:31,830
The Japan team finally finds a goal opportunity.

107
00:08:33,040 --> 00:08:36,500
Japan's tall forward Nagaoka goes for a header.

108
00:08:36,880 --> 00:08:39,340
So close! It hit the post.

109
00:08:40,880 --> 00:08:43,010
- Good shot.
- Thanks.

110
00:08:43,930 --> 00:08:45,010
Guys.

111
00:08:46,260 --> 00:08:48,760
We can still win this match.

112
00:08:49,470 --> 00:08:52,140
Paraguay flew a long way here.

113
00:08:52,230 --> 00:08:55,940
They are tired and slower in the second half than the first.

114
00:08:56,100 --> 00:09:00,440
There's a three-goal difference, but we definitely have a chance to win.

115
00:09:00,730 --> 00:09:02,440
H- He...

116
00:09:02,530 --> 00:09:08,280
When everyone gave up, this kid is still fighting for victory!

117
00:09:08,780 --> 00:09:11,790
First Nankatsu Middle School, then the Japanese youth...

118
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:14,120
He always carries the team to victory.

119
00:09:14,500 --> 00:09:16,460
That's Ozora Tsubasa!

120
00:09:17,290 --> 00:09:18,540
Alright, guys.

121
00:09:18,630 --> 00:09:22,550
Tsubasa is right, they are definitely tired.

122
00:09:23,050 --> 00:09:27,180
But we trained hard at camp to come here.

123
00:09:27,260 --> 00:09:29,600
Let's show our determination and win!

124
00:09:29,800 --> 00:09:30,890
Okay!

125
00:09:33,560 --> 00:09:35,230
So, can the Japan team

126
00:09:35,310 --> 00:09:39,310
turn the score around with Tsubasa?

127
00:09:48,740 --> 00:09:54,200
For Japan's victory, I must now take control of the midfield.

128
00:09:54,750 --> 00:09:57,960
Alright, the midfield is mine!

129
00:10:00,130 --> 00:10:01,130
What?

130
00:10:01,210 --> 00:10:04,510
Great, Tsubasa didn't just sit on the bench.

131
00:10:04,590 --> 00:10:06,840
He was studying the opponent's movements.

132
00:10:07,180 --> 00:10:09,430
Well done, kid.

133
00:10:09,510 --> 00:10:11,470
Advance!

134
00:10:11,550 --> 00:10:14,350
I want to fight using everything I've learned in my 15 years of football life!

135
00:10:15,890 --> 00:10:16,730
There it is!

136
00:10:16,810 --> 00:10:19,310
Ozora Tsubasa passes them on his own!

137
00:10:19,400 --> 00:10:21,110
What incredible dribbling!

138
00:10:32,620 --> 00:10:33,990
Towards adult football...

139
00:10:34,080 --> 00:10:36,870
And at the same time, world football.

140
00:10:37,660 --> 00:10:39,460
Tsubasa now...

141
00:10:41,580 --> 00:10:43,630
Go!

142
00:10:44,130 --> 00:10:45,510
Flew to new heights!

143
00:10:46,260 --> 00:10:48,380
Drive Shot!

144
00:10:50,090 --> 00:10:51,640
Goal!

145
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:54,810
Finally, Japan scores its first goal!

146
00:10:54,890 --> 00:10:56,310
I did it!

147
00:10:58,310 --> 00:11:01,150
Great Tsubasa. Your shot was awesome!

148
00:11:01,560 --> 00:11:02,860
Unique.

149
00:11:03,770 --> 00:11:06,650
Tsubasa, you are truly incredible!

150
00:11:12,910 --> 00:11:14,740
The game has turned.

151
00:11:15,490 --> 00:11:17,160
That's it, Tsubasa.

152
00:11:17,500 --> 00:11:20,040
This is what I was hoping for.

153
00:11:20,580 --> 00:11:23,460
You will change the Japan team.

154
00:11:25,800 --> 00:11:30,970
Japan has another goal opportunity, Tsubasa is at the free kick!

155
00:11:36,310 --> 00:11:41,350
In the net! Tsubasa takes a curving shot!

156
00:11:41,440 --> 00:11:43,730
Second goal!

157
00:11:45,060 --> 00:11:49,400
Great. His movements are getting faster.

158
00:11:50,070 --> 00:11:53,490
Tsubasa! Score one more!

159
00:12:14,840 --> 00:12:16,050
In the net!

160
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:19,930
Ozora Tsubasa scores the third goal with his special overhead kick!

161
00:12:20,020 --> 00:12:22,270
They've tied it with Paraguay!

162
00:12:22,350 --> 00:12:28,520
Ozora Tsubasa made an incredible hat-trick in his first match for Japan!

163
00:12:27,900 --> 00:12:30,740
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

164
00:12:33,670 --> 00:12:35,930
Japan Team | Born: July 28 | Blood Type: A

165
00:12:36,430 --> 00:12:40,180
He did it! Ozora Tsubasa made a hat-trick. A new star is born.

166
00:12:37,930 --> 00:12:40,180
This match ended in a draw.

167
00:12:40,300 --> 00:12:44,140
But Tsubasa was in the headlines the next day.

168
00:12:44,980 --> 00:12:49,060
The press declared him the savior of Japanese football...

169
00:12:49,150 --> 00:12:53,320
...and the new hero of Japanese football.

170
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:57,160
This was the beginning of the Tsubasa legend.

171
00:12:58,030 --> 00:12:59,780
Tsubasa took a big step.

172
00:12:59,870 --> 00:13:01,280
Then February came.

173
00:13:01,370 --> 00:13:03,540
The day his teammates

174
00:13:03,620 --> 00:13:05,660
saw their high school entrance exam results.

175
00:13:06,330 --> 00:13:13,210
Oh no, I can't look. I'm sure I'm the only one who didn't pass.

176
00:13:13,550 --> 00:13:15,590
What are you saying, Ishizaki?

177
00:13:15,670 --> 00:13:17,970
The kids from Otomo middle school are waiting there.

178
00:13:21,050 --> 00:13:22,970
Nankatsu High School

179
00:13:25,980 --> 00:13:28,980
Shizuoka Prefecture Nankatsu Public High School - Entrance Exam Acceptance List

180
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:33,780
M- My name isn't there!

181
00:13:33,860 --> 00:13:35,230
M- My name isn't there either.

182
00:13:35,740 --> 00:13:38,610
Are you sure, Ishizaki, Urabe?

183
00:13:38,700 --> 00:13:39,660
Yes.

184
00:13:39,740 --> 00:13:41,700
Only the two of us.

185
00:13:41,780 --> 00:13:43,240
We didn't pass.

186
00:13:43,660 --> 00:13:47,000
Hey, the waiting list is over here.

187
00:13:47,290 --> 00:13:48,540
Alright, let's go!

188
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:50,250
Please be there!

189
00:13:50,330 --> 00:13:57,260
Shizuoka Prefecture Nankatsu Public High School - Entrance Exam Waiting List

190
00:13:51,290 --> 00:13:52,750
There!

191
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:55,090
Both of us are on the waiting list.

192
00:13:55,170 --> 00:13:59,510
So if two people don't register, we'll get in!

193
00:13:59,590 --> 00:14:01,340
That's right.

194
00:14:01,930 --> 00:14:03,970
Yes!

195
00:14:04,060 --> 00:14:07,350
Hey, none of you are thinking of giving me your spot?

196
00:14:07,430 --> 00:14:12,440
If no one gives, I'll have to pick one of you.

197
00:14:12,520 --> 00:14:13,690
Hey, hey.

198
00:14:13,770 --> 00:14:15,690
Ishizaki, you seem to have gotten too serious.

199
00:14:15,780 --> 00:14:18,070
Musashi Medical School Affiliated High School - Admission Documents

200
00:14:18,150 --> 00:14:20,950
Tsubasa's friends and rivals,

201
00:14:21,030 --> 00:14:25,200
Each went their own way and finished middle school.

202
00:14:26,740 --> 00:14:28,040
And...

203
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:31,670
Hello.

204
00:14:32,210 --> 00:14:34,790
Sanae-chan, me too.

205
00:14:38,420 --> 00:14:41,050
What? You're going to Brazil tomorrow?

206
00:14:42,090 --> 00:14:42,930
Yes.

207
00:14:43,010 --> 00:14:44,800
Wh- Why so sudden?

208
00:14:45,220 --> 00:14:47,560
Graduation hasn't come yet.

209
00:14:48,100 --> 00:14:48,930
Yes.

210
00:14:49,600 --> 00:14:53,060
I was really very lucky.

211
00:14:54,310 --> 00:14:56,320
I found unique friends.

212
00:14:56,730 --> 00:14:58,990
And since my childhood

213
00:14:59,070 --> 00:15:02,950
I could dedicate myself to the football I love in the best possible conditions.

214
00:15:04,030 --> 00:15:05,530
And now...

215
00:15:05,620 --> 00:15:11,080
I must go to Brazil to realize my childhood dream.

216
00:15:12,420 --> 00:15:15,920
But when I go to Brazil, my friends won't be there.

217
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:19,800
I have to do everything on my own.

218
00:15:21,010 --> 00:15:24,590
That's why I want to leave Japan alone.

219
00:15:25,220 --> 00:15:28,010
Alone? But why?

220
00:15:28,510 --> 00:15:34,100
If everyone comes to see me off, I feel like I won't want to leave Japan.

221
00:15:35,650 --> 00:15:39,400
It's not that I'm not determined, I'm actually nervous.

222
00:15:39,900 --> 00:15:41,110
Tsubasa.

223
00:15:42,820 --> 00:15:44,030
But it's okay.

224
00:15:44,110 --> 00:15:47,620
When I arrive in Brazil, I'll dedicate myself completely to football.

225
00:15:47,990 --> 00:15:49,370
Please don't worry about me.

226
00:15:51,910 --> 00:15:52,750
Okay.

227
00:15:54,420 --> 00:15:58,840
I just wanted to say goodbye to you.

228
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:05,640
Like Wakabayashi, I don't plan to return to Japan without becoming a professional.

229
00:16:08,180 --> 00:16:09,640
Tsubasa.

230
00:16:10,680 --> 00:16:13,890
Then take care. Say goodbye to the others for me.

231
00:16:18,020 --> 00:16:18,900
Goodbye.

232
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:35,830
Finally, spring has arrived.

233
00:16:36,290 --> 00:16:38,500
Tsubasa, are you sure?

234
00:16:38,580 --> 00:16:40,420
Are you taking only this?

235
00:16:40,750 --> 00:16:44,920
Yes. I'm not going on a trip to Brazil.

236
00:16:45,430 --> 00:16:47,930
If I need something, I'll buy it there.

237
00:16:48,220 --> 00:16:51,060
Didn't you leave a bit early for the bus?

238
00:16:51,140 --> 00:16:53,430
Yes. Because today is my last day before I go.

239
00:16:53,520 --> 00:16:56,310
I'll take a quick tour around Nankatsu and then go.

240
00:16:56,980 --> 00:16:57,810
Okay.

241
00:16:58,650 --> 00:17:02,780
Alright, Mom, Dad, I'm going.

242
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:04,240
Okay.

243
00:17:04,320 --> 00:17:05,610
Take care.

244
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:15,410
He's finally going.

245
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:19,330
Tsubasa had been dreaming of this since childhood.

246
00:17:19,920 --> 00:17:24,210
I think the only thing we can do is watch over him.

247
00:17:25,130 --> 00:17:25,970
Yes.

248
00:17:27,970 --> 00:17:32,140
By the way, are you sure it's a good idea to keep this secret?

249
00:17:32,260 --> 00:17:33,180
What?

250
00:17:33,260 --> 00:17:35,730
Tsubasa is going to have a little sibling.

251
00:17:37,190 --> 00:17:38,270
It's okay.

252
00:17:38,350 --> 00:17:41,730
When Tsubasa returns, the three of us can surprise him together.

253
00:17:42,070 --> 00:17:43,570
You're right.

254
00:17:44,070 --> 00:17:48,740
But, a little sibling? Do you know it's going to be a boy?

255
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:55,500
Yes. There will be one more footballer.

256
00:17:56,250 --> 00:17:58,040
I don't know what to say.

257
00:17:58,120 --> 00:18:01,500
I guess we need to buy another football.

258
00:18:07,380 --> 00:18:10,680
This is the place where I met the Nankatsu kids.

259
00:18:16,350 --> 00:18:17,560
Wakabayashi

260
00:18:22,610 --> 00:18:24,230
Hey, how are you John?

261
00:18:24,320 --> 00:18:29,860
Like your father, I'm going abroad and will become a professional player.

262
00:18:30,320 --> 00:18:31,780
Take care, John.

263
00:18:32,120 --> 00:18:33,570
Live long, okay?

264
00:18:44,840 --> 00:18:46,380
Coach Shiroyama.

265
00:18:51,180 --> 00:18:52,510
Thank you for everything.

266
00:19:04,730 --> 00:19:06,730
Nankatsu - Otomo

267
00:19:09,740 --> 00:19:11,860
Train hard, my lowerclassmen.

268
00:19:12,820 --> 00:19:14,120
Coach Furuya.

269
00:19:15,740 --> 00:19:17,200
Thank you for everything.

270
00:19:21,120 --> 00:19:23,710
It's almost time. I have to go.

271
00:19:25,170 --> 00:19:27,710
Is it true that a great kid from Japan is coming?

272
00:19:27,960 --> 00:19:30,590
Right. They will learn a lot from him.

273
00:19:30,670 --> 00:19:32,260
But he's from Japan, isn't he?

274
00:19:32,340 --> 00:19:35,600
Is he really good at football? I can't believe it.

275
00:19:35,680 --> 00:19:39,600
Idiot, if Roberto says so, he's good.

276
00:19:40,270 --> 00:19:42,270
I'm waiting for you, Tsubasa.

277
00:20:01,950 --> 00:20:04,620
Sorry. I decided at the last minute to come see you off.

278
00:20:05,630 --> 00:20:08,340
No. I'm glad you came.

279
00:20:10,050 --> 00:20:10,880
Here.

280
00:20:11,460 --> 00:20:15,930
If you have room, take them. These are football shoes.

281
00:20:16,550 --> 00:20:19,720
I thought these would be perfect for you.

282
00:20:20,430 --> 00:20:23,020
Thank you. They will be very useful.

283
00:20:38,570 --> 00:20:40,580
Well, I'm going.

284
00:20:41,200 --> 00:20:42,040
Okay.

285
00:20:48,380 --> 00:20:49,290
Tsubasa!

286
00:20:50,380 --> 00:20:51,710
Your dream...

287
00:20:52,460 --> 00:20:54,300
...make it come true.

288
00:21:11,770 --> 00:21:15,820
The flight to São Paulo via Los Angeles will begin shortly.